# GitBook Sync Rules

## Critical Files (GitBook reads these)

| File | Purpose | Edit Policy |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `SUMMARY.md` | Sidebar navigation | Edit when articles change |
| `README.md` | Homepage | Do NOT edit (GitBook-managed) |
| `.gitbook.yaml` | Space config | Rarely edit |

## SUMMARY.md Format

```markdown
# Table of contents

## Getting Started

* [What is Intain Markets](01_What_is_Intain_Markets.md)
* [User Roles](02_User_Roles_and_Responsibilities.md)

## Pools & Loans

* [Pools Overview](05_Pools_Overview.md)
```

- Each article appears EXACTLY ONCE
- Use `## Section` for L1 categories
- Use `* [Title](filename.md)` for articles
- Nested items use indentation with `  *`
- The title in SUMMARY.md can differ from frontmatter title

## Frontmatter Requirements

```yaml
---
title: Required — displayed as page title
description: Required — used for SEO and preview cards
---
```

GitBook also supports (use sparingly):
- `icon:` — page icon (e.g., `icon: book-open`)
- `hidden: true` — hide from navigation
- `layout.width: wide` — wide page layout

## GitBook Markdown Extensions

### Hints (callout boxes)
```markdown
{% hint style="info" %}
Helpful tip or additional context.
{% endhint %}
```
Styles: `info` (blue), `warning` (yellow), `danger` (red), `success` (green)

### Tabs
```markdown
{% tabs %}
{% tab title="Issuer" %}
Issuer-specific content here.
{% endtab %}
{% tab title="Investor" %}
Investor-specific content here.
{% endtab %}
{% endtabs %}
```

### Steppers
```markdown
{% stepper %}
{% step %}
### Step 1: Create Deal
Click the Create Deal button...
{% endstep %}
{% step %}
### Step 2: Select Pool
Choose the pool to include...
{% endstep %}
{% endstepper %}
```

## Links

- Internal: `[Settlement](36_Settlement_and_NFT_Transfer.md)` (relative path)
- Cross-article anchors: `[Payment Rails](36_Settlement_and_NFT_Transfer.md#payment-rails)`
- External: `[Wormhole Bridge](https://wormhole.com)` (full URL)

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Don't use HTML tags (GitBook strips most HTML)
- ❌ Don't use `<details>` / `<summary>` — use GitBook expandable blocks instead
- ❌ Don't embed iframes or scripts
- ❌ Don't put OpenAPI specs inline — upload via GitBook API
- ❌ Don't edit README.md — it's GitBook's homepage file
- ❌ Don't use absolute paths for images — always relative
